data server storage consolidation,   In a data center, servers are arranged in a rack with n server slots. However, due to varying server installations, the servers are spread out across different slots. You want to consolidate the servers into consecutive slots to improve data access efficiency. Find the minimum number of moves required to place all the servers into consecutive slots. In 1 move you can move 1 book to any arbitrary position.

Function description

Complete the solve function in the editor below. It has the following parameter(s):

Name Type description

n


INTEGER

number of servers.

INTEGER ARRAY

a

contains n unique integers, representing the current positions of the servers in the rack.

Return

The function must return an INTEGER denoting the minimum number of moves required to place all the servers into consecutive slots.


Constraints

1 ≤n≤ 10^5



1≤≤ 10^9



Input format for debugging

The first line contains an integer, n, denoting the number of elements in a.

Each line i of then subsequent lines (where 0 <i<n) contains an integer describing "a[i]".



code:-


class Solution {
public:
    int solve(int n, vector<int>& a) {

        sort(a.begin(), a.end());

        int j = 0;
        int best = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            while (j < n && a[j] <= a[i] + n - 1) {
                j++;
            }

            best = max(best, j - i);
        }

        return n - best;
    }
};